1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,540
Akane, can you hear me?

2
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:06,180
I'm picking you up, okay?

3
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:51,760
The answer?

4
00:01:54,340 --> 00:01:54,820
No.

5
00:01:58,040 --> 00:02:00,460
Maybe his tutoring session is going overtime.

6
00:02:01,380 --> 00:02:04,540
Yeah, but even still, it's not like him to just leave us in the dark.

7
00:02:05,060 --> 00:02:06,980
Who knows, though? Maybe he's out with a girl.

8
00:02:06,980 --> 00:02:10,480
I mean, how suspicious was that call he got the other day?

9
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:13,820
Yamada's not that kind of character.

10
00:02:14,300 --> 00:02:16,420
You really don't get him, do you, Prez?

11
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:22,040
I'm telling you, if you don't stay on your toes and make your move soon, you're gonna lose him to some random girl.

12
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:28,240
I know that.

13
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:29,760
Hmm?

14
00:02:31,380 --> 00:02:34,260
I know. So don't pressure me like that.

15
00:02:36,980 --> 00:02:42,500
If it's tearing you up that badly inside, you might as well tell him how you feel.

16
00:02:43,160 --> 00:02:45,000
What's even holding you back at this point?

17
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:50,320
One of these days, he'll meet someone.

18
00:02:51,180 --> 00:02:52,720
I have a feeling that he will.

19
00:02:57,720 --> 00:02:58,780
Excuse me, Yamada.

20
00:02:59,140 --> 00:03:00,320
Do you know G.O.S.E.?

21
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:01,860
It's a popular FPS game.

22
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:02,920
You play it, right?

23
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:06,160
Last night around 10pm, you matched against me.

24
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:06,880
Do you remember?

25
00:03:06,880 --> 00:03:11,680
In-game, I'm YTO3.

26
00:03:12,140 --> 00:03:15,280
But my real name is Yukari Tsubaki, and I'm from Class D.

27
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:19,160
If it's alright with you, I'd like you to show me how you play.

28
00:03:21,940 --> 00:03:22,760
But why?

29
00:03:23,160 --> 00:03:25,020
I just have my reasons, that's why.

30
00:03:26,020 --> 00:03:28,000
She totally thinks you cheated, bro.

31
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:35,260
Leave when you're done, okay?

32
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:36,360
Of course.

33
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:39,940
Hey, Tsubaki, you should watch my epic gameplay later, too.

34
00:03:39,940 --> 00:04:05,980
The truth is, I was a little suspicious.

35
00:04:06,600 --> 00:04:09,200
I didn't think anyone could play like that with sheer skill.

36
00:04:09,200 --> 00:04:15,400
But I misjudged you.

37
00:04:15,780 --> 00:04:16,620
I'm sorry.

38
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:17,720
I was wrong.

39
00:04:18,480 --> 00:04:19,720
Your skills are amazing.

40
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:22,600
Shouldn't you be playing professionally?

41
00:04:31,100 --> 00:04:32,980
Just like how I met you then.

42
00:04:32,980 --> 00:04:40,080
I know that one day,

43
00:04:40,980 --> 00:04:44,180
you'll meet someone, too.

44
00:04:44,180 --> 00:05:05,200
For someone with such arresting good lucks, he's quiet and reserved.

45
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:10,040
For someone who speaks so bluntly, he's actually pretty thoughtful.

46
00:05:11,160 --> 00:05:14,660
Anybody who's good friends with him knows that well.

47
00:05:14,660 --> 00:05:16,660
And also...

48
00:05:16,660 --> 00:05:18,580
Yamada?

49
00:05:18,580 --> 00:05:24,480
When we worked together on the committee last week, you were really a major help to me.

50
00:05:24,480 --> 00:05:25,480
So I, uh...

51
00:05:25,480 --> 00:05:26,560
So I, uh...

52
00:05:26,560 --> 00:05:28,380
Uh, have you and I ever spoken?

53
00:05:29,380 --> 00:05:31,680
That you can be a little cruel.

54
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:37,640
Hey, did you hear Miss Shirai-shi from class D finally confessed her feelings to Yamada?

55
00:05:37,640 --> 00:05:38,640
For real?

56
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:40,800
But of course she got shot down.

57
00:05:41,040 --> 00:05:41,580
No way.

58
00:05:41,700 --> 00:05:43,720
If Miss Shirai-shi can't get him, who can?

59
00:05:43,940 --> 00:05:45,940
Maybe he's not into girls.

60
00:05:46,020 --> 00:05:46,760
You think so?

61
00:05:46,920 --> 00:05:48,740
Come on, that would be such a waste.

62
00:05:48,860 --> 00:05:49,240
Right?

63
00:05:49,240 --> 00:05:56,400
We're second years, and you still don't have a girlfriend.

64
00:05:57,520 --> 00:06:01,420
If you stay single with your popularity, there are bound to be false rumors.

65
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:05,860
Why should I care what other people say?

66
00:06:06,200 --> 00:06:07,000
It doesn't matter.

67
00:06:07,800 --> 00:06:09,260
Oh, well, I get what you mean.

68
00:06:09,580 --> 00:06:12,060
But I felt bad seeing people spread lies about you.

69
00:06:12,880 --> 00:06:14,040
Don't you have a type?

70
00:06:14,920 --> 00:06:15,800
Not really.

71
00:06:16,420 --> 00:06:18,400
Surely even you must have some idea.

72
00:06:18,400 --> 00:06:19,400
I don't.

73
00:06:20,620 --> 00:06:22,200
Then who was your first crush-

74
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:22,720
I mean it.

75
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:26,820
There's no one.

76
00:06:28,080 --> 00:06:28,960
He sighed.

77
00:06:31,320 --> 00:06:32,100
Sorry about that.

78
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:32,440
Oh, no.

79
00:06:32,780 --> 00:06:33,180
I am.

80
00:06:33,500 --> 00:06:35,040
I shouldn't have pushed you like that.

81
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:39,420
I feel bad.

82
00:06:40,240 --> 00:06:41,400
So, um...

83
00:06:42,320 --> 00:06:43,400
Uh...

84
00:06:43,400 --> 00:06:44,400
Um...

85
00:06:44,400 --> 00:06:45,400
It's just...

86
00:06:46,060 --> 00:06:47,440
Come to think of it.

87
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:52,440
Years ago, there was a girl who confessed that she liked me.

88
00:06:53,340 --> 00:06:56,160
Back then, she got bullied like crazy.

89
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:56,800
Huh?

90
00:06:57,220 --> 00:06:59,960
It got pretty bad, so she stopped coming to school.

91
00:06:59,960 --> 00:07:11,320
But since I lived nearby, our teacher would send me to her house with handouts, and that's how we became friends.

92
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:18,140
However, when she did come to school, she said if I wasn't there, she felt like she didn't belong.

93
00:07:18,140 --> 00:07:21,920
So I tried to stay by her side, so I tried to stay by her side as much as I could.

94
00:07:24,480 --> 00:07:28,080
Then, are you saying that you liked that girl too, Yamada?

95
00:07:32,080 --> 00:07:32,480
Akito...

96
00:07:32,480 --> 00:07:36,640
Let's stay together forever, even after we're all grown up.

97
00:07:37,420 --> 00:07:39,320
I can't promise you that.

98
00:07:41,520 --> 00:07:44,200
I only did all that because our teacher told me to.

99
00:07:45,140 --> 00:07:46,460
That's all there was to it.

100
00:07:46,460 --> 00:07:55,040
The bullying never stopped, so she ended up transferring out.

101
00:07:57,460 --> 00:08:00,400
Although, sometimes, I think of her.

102
00:08:00,400 --> 00:08:07,740
The last time we spoke, I made her cry pretty hard.

103
00:08:08,820 --> 00:08:13,580
And I have moments where I'm left wondering, what would have been the right thing to say.

104
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:18,200
But I still don't know.

105
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:23,680
And now, it seems like such a drag.

106
00:08:26,100 --> 00:08:29,780
Since then, I've never been comfortable around girls.

107
00:08:30,400 --> 00:08:35,620
I see.

108
00:08:36,120 --> 00:08:39,940
The reality is, this guy doesn't have much interest in himself.

109
00:08:41,380 --> 00:08:45,260
That would explain why he doesn't really notice when other people care about him.

110
00:08:46,460 --> 00:08:49,960
Either that, or he's been deliberately averting his gaze from them.

111
00:08:52,260 --> 00:08:54,120
And did he say it was a drag?

112
00:08:54,620 --> 00:08:55,560
How scary.

113
00:08:56,580 --> 00:08:58,960
I'd better make sure I don't fall for this guy.

114
00:09:00,400 --> 00:09:05,940
If I ever fall in love with someone as cruel as him, I'll definitely be hurt someday.

115
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:08,180
I don't want that.

116
00:09:08,180 --> 00:09:16,300
Order delivery.

117
00:09:17,040 --> 00:09:19,000
Akane, can you drink some water?

118
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:23,480
Just try.

119
00:09:23,960 --> 00:09:25,040
Even if it's a little bit.

120
00:09:25,040 --> 00:09:38,440
She's burning up.

121
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:42,760
This fever, it's really bad.

122
00:09:44,760 --> 00:09:45,400
Cold.

123
00:09:46,040 --> 00:09:47,060
So cold.

124
00:09:47,060 --> 00:10:00,020
I feel awful.

125
00:10:01,020 --> 00:10:02,380
I'm so hot.

126
00:10:03,200 --> 00:10:04,180
I'm cold.

127
00:10:06,840 --> 00:10:08,560
What's going on?

128
00:10:09,240 --> 00:10:13,120
Behind my eyes, my head is spinning.

129
00:10:13,120 --> 00:10:16,240
I don't get it.

130
00:10:16,980 --> 00:10:20,080
What's happening to me right now?

131
00:10:22,540 --> 00:10:22,860
Akane.

132
00:10:23,680 --> 00:10:24,240
Akane?

133
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:25,960
Akane.

134
00:10:28,960 --> 00:10:31,480
Where's your card for your health insurance?

135
00:10:32,360 --> 00:10:34,440
Health insurance?

136
00:10:34,440 --> 00:10:35,900
Insurance card.

137
00:10:37,600 --> 00:10:38,280
And...

138
00:10:38,280 --> 00:10:40,400
My bag.

139
00:10:43,900 --> 00:10:44,340
Huh?

140
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:46,120
Hold on.

141
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:49,920
I could have sworn Yamada was just here.

142
00:10:52,160 --> 00:10:54,680
Am I imagining things?

143
00:10:54,680 --> 00:10:56,800
Miss Kinoshita?

144
00:10:57,500 --> 00:10:58,520
Can you hear me?

145
00:10:59,100 --> 00:10:59,660
Yeah.

146
00:11:01,400 --> 00:11:03,680
Why did it get...

147
00:11:03,680 --> 00:11:05,900
So noisy around me?

148
00:11:05,900 --> 00:11:06,020
Okay.

149
00:11:13,020 --> 00:11:13,780
Huh?

150
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:15,960
What time...

151
00:11:15,960 --> 00:11:16,940
Is it now?

152
00:11:18,060 --> 00:11:18,680
Did I...

153
00:11:19,580 --> 00:11:21,580
Fall asleep after that?

154
00:11:21,580 --> 00:11:26,400
I guess I never made it to the store, did I?

155
00:11:27,300 --> 00:11:31,920
On the bright side, though, I think I'm starting to feel a tiny bit better.

156
00:11:35,620 --> 00:11:36,220
Huh?

157
00:11:45,340 --> 00:11:45,940
Huh?

158
00:11:49,580 --> 00:11:50,140
Huh?

159
00:11:51,580 --> 00:11:52,580
Why?

160
00:11:54,300 --> 00:11:55,580
Why is he...

161
00:11:57,040 --> 00:11:57,540
Why?

162
00:12:04,220 --> 00:12:05,560
It's cold.

163
00:12:09,220 --> 00:12:12,900
Why are you here?

164
00:12:16,340 --> 00:12:17,900
I see.

165
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:18,700
It's a dream.

166
00:12:18,940 --> 00:12:19,600
I'm cold.

167
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:28,580
So you can stand on your feet again.

168
00:12:29,280 --> 00:12:30,040
How are you feeling?

169
00:12:31,320 --> 00:12:31,660
Huh?

170
00:12:32,020 --> 00:12:33,240
A bit surprised.

171
00:12:33,520 --> 00:12:34,720
I didn't mean it that way.

172
00:12:34,840 --> 00:12:35,100
Wait!

173
00:12:35,160 --> 00:12:35,880
It's not a dream!

174
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:36,700
Why are you here?

175
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:38,020
I mean, you can't catch this!

176
00:12:39,540 --> 00:12:42,680
I'll explain it all to you in a moment, so go back to bed for now.

177
00:12:43,520 --> 00:12:44,700
You couldn't even drink water.

178
00:12:44,880 --> 00:12:46,300
You were in critical condition, you know.

179
00:12:46,300 --> 00:12:49,520
Okay.

180
00:12:55,680 --> 00:12:56,280
Okay...

181
00:12:56,280 --> 00:12:57,280
How are you feeling now?

182
00:12:57,280 --> 00:13:04,160
um actually when i woke up earlier i thought i was feeling a little better

183
00:13:04,160 --> 00:13:11,480
well i'm really glad to hear that when i got here you had collapsed by the bike racks

184
00:13:11,480 --> 00:13:18,040
did i really come to think of it i do remember thinking i saw someone that looked like yamada

185
00:13:18,040 --> 00:13:25,160
that means it really was yamada who helped me but you seemed really sick so

186
00:13:25,160 --> 00:13:29,520
did he come all the way here to check on me because he was worried

187
00:13:29,520 --> 00:13:35,460
there's a chance he could have caught my cold himself but he stayed with me anyway

188
00:13:35,460 --> 00:13:41,620
why would he go out of his way to be so nice to someone like me

189
00:13:41,620 --> 00:13:54,580
thank you i'm so grateful yamada you don't know how exhausted i was

190
00:13:54,580 --> 00:14:01,520
you really saved my life i mean it i have no idea how i'll ever repay you for this

191
00:14:01,520 --> 00:14:02,700
you're an angel

192
00:14:02,700 --> 00:14:04,020
yeah sure

193
00:14:04,020 --> 00:14:06,660
anyway as i was saying

194
00:14:06,660 --> 00:14:11,800
i'm so sorry for saying you were cold but really you're such a kind person

195
00:14:11,800 --> 00:14:13,660
did she ever say that to me

196
00:14:13,660 --> 00:14:16,820
the truth is you've always been kind from the moment

197
00:14:16,820 --> 00:14:18,560
if you keep reaching over you'll fall

198
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:21,660
i'm sorry i stepped on it

199
00:14:21,660 --> 00:14:24,780
oh yeah that book

200
00:14:24,780 --> 00:14:29,400
i didn't have anything to do so i borrowed it and started reading

201
00:14:29,400 --> 00:14:34,840
is a good book huh it totally saved me after the whole heartbreak thing you know

202
00:14:34,840 --> 00:14:36,800
i didn't really get it

203
00:14:36,800 --> 00:14:39,780
it's not exactly something you could relate to

204
00:14:39,780 --> 00:14:43,200
since i'm pretty sure you're the side who does the dumping yamada

205
00:14:43,200 --> 00:14:44,960
no i wouldn't say that

206
00:14:44,960 --> 00:14:46,000
oh come on now

207
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:48,600
this illness really has you keyed up and scary

208
00:14:48,600 --> 00:14:55,680
well i'm sure the emotional strain is tough for the dumpers too

209
00:14:55,680 --> 00:14:59,360
but you're especially kind so it'd be really draining

210
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:06,180
i'm not

211
00:15:06,180 --> 00:15:09,760
i'm not the good guy you think i am

212
00:15:09,760 --> 00:15:11,760
at all

213
00:15:11,760 --> 00:15:17,760
that's the same look takuma gave me

214
00:15:17,760 --> 00:15:21,180
like he was sorry and in pain

215
00:15:21,180 --> 00:15:23,920
and like he wished he could just disappear

216
00:15:23,920 --> 00:15:25,780
but it's all right though

217
00:15:25,780 --> 00:15:26,960
i'm okay with it

218
00:15:26,960 --> 00:15:28,240
that's romance

219
00:15:28,240 --> 00:15:31,340
even though he cheated on you

220
00:15:31,340 --> 00:15:32,740
well

221
00:15:32,740 --> 00:15:35,380
now that it's in the past

222
00:15:35,380 --> 00:15:38,940
sometimes i'm glad he was up front about dumping me

223
00:15:38,940 --> 00:15:40,580
instead of keeping up a lie

224
00:15:40,580 --> 00:15:43,140
sorry akane

225
00:15:43,140 --> 00:15:47,280
at least i ended up not having to feel truly humiliated

226
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:49,020
sorry

227
00:15:49,020 --> 00:15:50,380
sorry

228
00:15:50,380 --> 00:15:53,280
i knew nothing i said would change his mind

229
00:15:53,280 --> 00:15:54,800
so to make it easier

230
00:15:54,800 --> 00:15:56,920
i just accepted the breakup right away

231
00:15:56,920 --> 00:15:58,820
okay

232
00:15:58,820 --> 00:15:58,860
okay

233
00:15:58,860 --> 00:16:00,880
someday

234
00:16:00,880 --> 00:16:03,500
when i've become a memory he looks back on

235
00:16:03,500 --> 00:16:06,360
i'd rather he remembered me with a smile on my face

236
00:16:06,360 --> 00:16:08,740
instead of frowning and all teary-eyed

237
00:16:08,740 --> 00:16:11,620
i want him to think of me like

238
00:16:11,620 --> 00:16:13,920
i really shouldn't have let her go

239
00:16:13,920 --> 00:16:14,880
she was great

240
00:16:14,880 --> 00:16:19,200
that's a lot better don't you think

241
00:16:19,200 --> 00:16:26,200
did you feel

242
00:16:26,200 --> 00:16:28,840
sorry for me

243
00:16:28,840 --> 00:16:31,660
goodbye

244
00:16:31,660 --> 00:16:33,660
akito

245
00:16:33,660 --> 00:16:42,280
i'm sorry

246
00:16:42,280 --> 00:16:44,940
but you were always there for me

247
00:16:44,940 --> 00:16:46,480
so thank you

248
00:16:46,480 --> 00:16:50,140
take care

249
00:16:50,140 --> 00:16:50,700
goodbye

250
00:16:50,700 --> 00:17:10,260
i guess that's right

251
00:17:10,260 --> 00:17:27,280
did it go down

252
00:17:27,280 --> 00:17:28,680
yeah

253
00:17:28,680 --> 00:17:30,260
yeah i think it did a little

254
00:17:30,260 --> 00:17:31,240
yamada

255
00:17:31,240 --> 00:17:34,040
is it okay if i eat some of that yogurt you bought earlier

256
00:17:34,040 --> 00:17:34,960
yeah sure

257
00:17:34,960 --> 00:17:42,340
are those tears of joy or

258
00:17:42,340 --> 00:17:44,240
it's tasty but it kills to swallow

259
00:17:44,240 --> 00:17:45,240
oh

260
00:17:45,240 --> 00:17:51,000
if it was anyone other than yamada sitting there when i woke up

261
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:53,820
i would have definitely had a panic attack

262
00:17:53,820 --> 00:17:56,920
but what's this vibe he's giving off

263
00:17:56,920 --> 00:17:59,940
for some reason i feel so safe and secure

264
00:17:59,940 --> 00:18:04,340
well i bet it must have been an ordeal for him

265
00:18:04,340 --> 00:18:07,220
he's uncomfortable around women as it is

266
00:18:07,220 --> 00:18:10,080
thanks for the yogurt

267
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:11,860
could you put this on the table

268
00:18:11,860 --> 00:18:13,160
sure

269
00:18:13,160 --> 00:18:18,320
oh crap

270
00:18:18,320 --> 00:18:19,380
huh

271
